he left has an open shutter that's a window leaf; behind it is the window opening. So that's window 1. Middle arched = window 2. Right arched = window 3. Yes 3.\n\nThus [3].\n\nI'll write a brief self-contained answer.\n</think>\n\nLooking across the room, there are three window units set into the wall: one on the left (with its leaf swung open), one arched window in the center, and one arched window on the right.\n\n[3]<|im_end|>",
